From 1b700b3a929a960a104ebb762459227ebba4b2c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Devoogdt <thomas@devoogdt.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:06:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] meson: do not drop lib_tcolors when no curses library is
 found

The curses_libs loop variable is used as a dependency of lib_tcolors.
When none of slang, ncursesw and ncurses is found, the loop finishes
with curses_libs being the ncurses disabler, because it is built with
"disabler : true". The disabler propagates to lib_tcolors, which then
silently disappears, together with every target linking to it:
dmesg, hexdump, lsblk and sfdisk.

Only pass curses_libs to lib_tcolors when a library was found. This
matches the autotools build, where these tools do not need curses.

Upstream: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/pull/4743
Signed-off-by: Thomas Devoogdt <thomas@devoogdt.com>
---
 lib/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/meson.build b/lib/meson.build
index 25febbc19..7d931523a 100644
--- a/lib/meson.build
+++ b/lib/meson.build
@@ -105,6 +105,6 @@ lib_tcolors = static_library(
   'tcolors',
   lib_color_sources,
   include_directories : dir_include,
-  dependencies : curses_libs)
+  dependencies : curses_libs.found() ? curses_libs : [])
 
 lib_tcolors_manadocs = files('terminal-colors.d.5.adoc')
